  "manual_review": [
    "New cast, environment and props use a coherent palette, material and light language; characters and scene remain recognizably the same across the eight frames.",
    "After the targeted resize, the stone body is visibly separated from wooden pier ends; solid clamp-like guide bars are removed and thin slack lateral guides remain. This clears the causal readability defect at concept level.",
    "Crossing frame places Marfa feet on the stone; arrival frame places her at the bakery. The victory copy claims arrival rather than an already animated door opening.",
    "All four schematic observer views match the documented truth table: side variants show support, front-tall hides the stone, front-folded shows stone while hiding support.",
    "Proof, law and arrival remain distinct. The Atlas records the visible stage image without requiring belief erasure, and load support is stated before crossing.",
    "Phone-size frames retain uncut essential text and clear primary controls. Main-frame enabled button targets meet the tested 44 CSS pixel minimum at 844x390."
  ],
  "resolved_findings": [
    {
      "id": "R01",
      "severity": "major",
      "issue": "Stone rings and thick vertical guide bars visually merged with piers, making an ordinary supported bridge plausible.",
      "resolution": "Stone and float reduced/recentered; thick bars removed; final water gaps and slack lateral guides inspected."
    },
    {
      "id": "R02",
      "severity": "major",
      "issue": "Success replay hit area was only about 19.5 CSS px high at 844x390.",
      "resolution": "Replay receives a 90 logical pixel minimum height, about 48.7 CSS px after scaling; remains inside the frame."
    },
    {
      "id": "R03",
      "severity": "major",
      "issue": "Undo reset the initial fixture although the spec promised previous-step undo.",
      "resolution": "True one-step placement/form history is implemented and tested."
    },
    {
      "id": "R04",
      "severity": "major",
      "issue": "An in-frame arrival button added an unnecessary second mandatory click after ordering the crossing.",
      "resolution": "Live crossing automatically completes; pause holds it, resume completes it; capture mode keeps a storyboard frame through external review navigation."
    },
    {
      "id": "R05",
      "severity": "minor",
      "issue": "A floating law label obscured Plum face.",
      "resolution": "Law-only Plum position moved; final large and phone frames inspected."
    },
    {
      "id": "R06",
      "severity": "minor",
      "issue": "Browser requested a missing favicon.",
      "resolution": "Embedded icon added; final pass records zero console and HTTP errors."
    }
  ],
  "measurement_corrections": "Initial scrollHeight overflow flags were caused by decorative speech tails. Actual text Range bounds and screenshot inspection confirm text is contained; these were test false positives, not hidden product errors.",
  "limitations": [
    "This is an owner-review design proposal, not user approval, a physical-device test, or evidence of fun or unaided comprehension by fresh players.",
    "Observer views are illustrated discrete presets. General geometric raycasting, collision, fluid/load simulation and Godot integration are not implemented or validated here.",
    "Thin guides are documented as lateral restraints that do not bear weight; the final concept drawing is not a physical engineering proof.",
    "Character cutouts provide a concept pose rather than a complete animation or direction set; movement and object contact need production assets later.",
    "The second puzzle is a narrative teaser, not a completed playable level. The package does not validate later monetization, retention or graphics integrations."
  ],
